template:
Create one photorealistic portrait for the German-Arab Chamber of Industry and Commerce (AHK Egypt) 75th anniversary photobooth. The input image is the sole identity reference.
{{SUBJECT_DESCRIPTION}}
Keep EVERY participant and the exact number of people. Preserve their facial identity, apparent age, natural skin tone, eye shape, eyelid folds, eyebrows, nose, jaw, lips, smile geometry, wrinkles, moles, facial hair, hair texture, expression and gaze. Do not beautify, smooth skin, morph or average faces, reshape faces, invent people, or change expressions. Keep each person immediately recognizable.
Change ONLY attire and environment. Clothing: {{OUTFIT}}
Preserve any religious or cultural headcover that is visible in the input, naturally draped, coordinated with the outfit. Preserve exposed hair when no headcover is present. Every person must have opaque clothing covering torso, chest and shoulders. Retain individual clothing preferences; use local gender estimates only as outfit guidance and defer to the photo.
Environment: {{SCENE}}
Output a single coherent 2:3 portrait, never a collage. Match the reference pose and framing. Keep all faces inside the central safe area, at least 15% from the top and 12% from the sides for the anniversary frame. Use natural skin texture, convincing lighting and shadows, print-friendly brightness and realistic hands. No added text, dates, logos, watermark, border, spacesuits, robotic armor or extra people. An anniversary frame will be applied separately.
